3. Warmed UpProblem: "What is 0x3D (base 16) in decimal (base 10) 
Hexadecimal is base-16. To convert 0x3D to decimal, multiply the position values: \((3 \times 16^1) + (D \times 16^0)\).
Since D = 13 in hex, the math is 48 + 13 = 61.
